 "title": {
  "raw": "CREATING A SYSTEM DASHBOARD IN DYNAMICS 365",
  "rendered": "CREATING A SYSTEM DASHBOARD IN DYNAMICS 365"
 },
 "content": {
  "raw": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To create a system dashboard, go to the Power Apps Maker and create a new solution:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24547} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd77f19e248.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24547\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Then select New-&gt;Dashboard and select the type of dashboard:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24548} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd78158b256.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24548\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We will select 2-column overview:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24549} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd78396e05d.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24549\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Give the dashboard a name:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24550} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd785b8dd09.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24550\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>And we will add a list to the first component:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24551} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd787445740.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24551\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It will be a list of all Accounts:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24552} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd789abe03b.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24552\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click Save:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24553} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd78b60b240.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24553\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If I don’t publish, we can see the Dashboard under Dashboards, however we see the message “Dashboard has no components to be shown. Please add one or more components”:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":1194,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://thepowerappsninja.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/img_5df3c8bfc4c080-840x507.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1194\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Let’s Publish the dashboard back in the Maker page:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24556} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd7a6c335ad.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24556\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We now see the dashboard:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":3328,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://thepowerappsninja.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Capture-27-840x557.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3328\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We can restrict access to the dashboard through Security Roles:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24558} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd7ac2d3428.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24558\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":24559} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd7ad82e436.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24559\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href=\"https://thepowerappsninja.com/2024/02/29/using-calendar-control-in-dynamics-365-power-apps-dashboard-components/\" title=\"\">CREATING A SYSTEM DASHBOARD IN DYNAMICS 365</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@powerappsninja\">https://www.youtube.com/@powerappsninja</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
  "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To create a system dashboard, go to the Power Apps Maker and create a new solution:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd77f19e248.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24547\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Then select New-&gt;Dashboard and select the type of dashboard:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd78158b256.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24548\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We will select 2-column overview:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd78396e05d.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24549\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Give the dashboard a name:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd785b8dd09.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24550\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And we will add a list to the first component:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd787445740.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24551\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It will be a list of all Accounts:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd789abe03b.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24552\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Click Save:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd78b60b240.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24553\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If I don’t publish, we can see the Dashboard under Dashboards, however we see the message “Dashboard has no components to be shown. Please add one or more components”:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"840\" height=\"507\" src=\"https://thepowerappsninja.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/img_5df3c8bfc4c080-840x507.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1194\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let’s Publish the dashboard back in the Maker page:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd7a6c335ad.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24556\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We now see the dashboard:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"840\" height=\"557\" src=\"https://thepowerappsninja.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Capture-27-840x557.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3328\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We can restrict access to the dashboard through Security Roles:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd7ac2d3428.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24558\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://carldesouza.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/img_5fcd7ad82e436.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-24559\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://thepowerappsninja.com/2024/02/29/using-calendar-control-in-dynamics-365-power-apps-dashboard-components/\" title=\"\">CREATING A SYSTEM DASHBOARD IN DYNAMICS 365</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@powerappsninja\">https://www.youtube.com/@powerappsninja</a></p>\n",
  "protected": false,
  "block_version": 1
 },
